 36S  dL E$Least-squares fitting is done by GLSC (version 23-Sep-2026)          
 36S  c  1972Sa09: E=3.1 MeV triton beam with an intensity of |?250 nA was      
 36S 2c  provided from the 3.5-MV Van de Graaff accelerator at Brookhaven       
 36S 3c  National Laboratory. Targets were 187-|mg/cm{+2} and 400-|mg/cm{+2}    
 36S 4c  Sb{-2}S{-3} enriched to 86% in {+34}S on 127-|mm Mo backings. Protons  
 36S 5c  from {+34}S(t,p|g){+36}S were detected using a 1-mm-thick annular Si   
 36S 6c  detector covering 165|'-175|'. |g rays were detected using a coaxial   
 36S 7c  25-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector, rotatable to 0|', 45|', and 90|'. Measured  
 36S 8c  E{-p}, I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, and p|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p,  
 36S 9c  |g-ray multipolarities, and lifetimes from DSAM lineshape analysis.    
 36S  c  1971Ol02: E=3.12, 3.28, and 3.40 MeV triton beams with an intensity of 
 36S 2c  |?40 nA were produced from the 3.5-MV Van de Graaff accelerator at     
 36S 3c  Brookhaven National Laboratory. Targets were 200-600-|mg/cm{+2}        
 36S 4c  Sb{-2}S{-3} enriched to 85.61% in {+34}S on 70-|mg/cm{+2} Mo,          
 36S 5c  2-mg/cm{+2} Au, or 1.7-mg/cm{+2} Ni backings. Protons from             
 36S 6c  {+34}S(t,p|g){+36}S were detected using a 900-|mm-thick annular Si     
 36S 7c  detector covering 165|'-170|', and at 135|' using a Si detector with   
 36S 8c  FWHM=30 keV. |g rays were detected using a 5|*6-in. NaI(Tl) detector at
 36S 9c  0|'-90|' and a 40-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector at 0|'-140|' with FWHM=1.9    
 36S Ac  keV. Internal pairs were detected using an intermediate-image pair     
 36S Bc  spectrometer. 511-keV annihilation |g rays were detected using a       
 36S Cc  3|*2-in. plastic scintillator in delayed coincidence. Measured E{-p},  
 36S Dc  I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p, and   
 36S Ec  |g-ray multipolarities. 1971Ol02 and 1972Sa09 were done by the same    
 36S Fc  leading author.                                                        
 36S  c  1971Ju02: E=3.1 MeV triton beam with an intensity of |?80 nA was       
 36S 2c  provided from the 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator at the Nuclear        
 36S 3c  Research Center in Strasbourg, France. The target was a 500-|mg/cm{+2} 
 36S 4c  Sb{-2}S{-3} layer enriched to 85% in {+34}S on a 30-|mm Mo backing.    
 36S 5c  Protons from {+34}S(t,p|g){+36}S were detected using an annular        
 36S 6c  200-mm{+2}, 1-mm-thick Si detector. |g rays were detected using a      
 36S 7c  Compton polarimeter consisting of a central 3.8-cm-dia, 7.6-cm NaI(Tl) 
 36S 8c  detector at 90|' and two 7.6|*7.6-cm NaI(Tl) detectors parallel and    
 36S 9c  perpendicular to the reaction plane. Measured p-|g-Compton triple      
 36S Ac  coincidences and linear polarizations. Deduced levels, J, |p, and      
 36S Bc  |g-ray multipolarities.                                                
 36S  c  1979Fo17: measured |s(|q) for {+34}S(t,p){+36}S g.s. at E=15 MeV.      
